## Code samples

### curl

```sh
curl -X PUT '{{base_url}}/raw' -H 'Content-Type: application/octet-stream' --data-binary '@bodies/data/report.csv' -L
```

### httpie

```sh
http --follow -- PUT '{{base_url}}/raw' \
  'Content-Type:application/octet-stream' \
  < bodies/data/report.csv
```

### fetch

```js
import { openAsBlob } from "node:fs";

const BASE_URL = "{{base_url}}";

const response = await fetch(BASE_URL + "/raw", {
  method: "PUT",
  headers: {
    "Content-Type": "application/octet-stream",
  },
  body: await openAsBlob("bodies/data/report.csv"),
});
console.log(response.status);
console.log(await response.text());
```

### python

```python
import requests

BASE_URL = "{{base_url}}"

response = requests.put(
    BASE_URL + "/raw",
    data=open("bodies/data/report.csv", "rb"),
    headers={
        "Content-Type": "application/octet-stream",
    },
)
print(response.status_code)
print(response.text)
```

### rust

```rust
// Cargo.toml: reqwest = { version = "0.12", features = ["blocking"] }

const BASE_URL: &str = "{{base_url}}";

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let client = reqwest::blocking::Client::builder()
        .build()?;
    let response = client
        .request(reqwest::Method::PUT, [BASE_URL, "/raw"].concat())
        .header("Content-Type", "application/octet-stream")
        .body(std::fs::File::open("bodies/data/report.csv")?)
        .send()?;
    println!("{}", response.status());
    println!("{}", response.text()?);
    Ok(())
}
```
